@startuml
title beginDurableRunUnderGrant — the atomic join, branch by branch, each abort to its error code
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FBFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #294C60
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #38789E
  LifeLineBorderColor #6A92AA
  GroupBackgroundColor #FFF3E8
  GroupBorderColor #D97638
}

participant "Signed deploy\n(channel wallet)" as Deploy #C8E6DC
participant "beginDurableRunUnderGrant\nclause" as Clause #FFE4A6
participant "runsCh + grantsCh\n(joined state)" as State #FFE4A6
participant "Embers send handler\n(abort classifier)" as API #FFC9A8

Deploy -> Clause : run_id, grant_id, agents_team,\ncreated_at, definition + artifact hashes
Clause -> Clause : deployData -> (timestamp, deployerId);\nrevAddress(deployerId) -> signer address

Clause -> State : **one join**: for(address; @runs <- runsCh;\n@grants <- grantsCh) -- both states taken\natomically; nothing interleaves until\nboth are put back
note right of State #FFF0C7
This is why grants live INSIDE the
agents-teams env: a separate env would
reintroduce revocation races and
split-brain day counters.
end note

alt grants does not contain grant_id
Clause --> API : abort "grant not found"
API --> API : re-read grant -> **404 grant_not_found**
else runs already contains run_id (resend)
Clause -> Clause : verify identity: owner == grantor,\ngrant_id, team, created_at, all five hashes
alt identical
Clause --> API : acknowledge true -- **idempotent:\nthe day counter is NOT incremented again**
else any field differs
Clause --> API : abort "run identity conflict" -> 500
end
else grant.revoked
Clause --> API : abort "grant is revoked"
API --> API : re-read grant -> **403 grant_revoked**
else grant.grantee != signer address
Clause --> API : abort "grant grantee mismatch"\n(the chain checks the SIGNER; the HTTP\nprincipal check is the channel's fail-fast half)
API --> API : surviving live grant -> 500 internal_error
else grant.agents_team != agents_team
Clause --> API : abort "grant team mismatch" -> 500
else cap check, only now
Clause -> Clause : match caps.max_runs_per_day:\nNil -> admit untouched;\nelse compare runs_today.day to\n<latex>\lfloor timestamp / 86\,400\,000 \rfloor</latex>
alt same day, count < cap
Clause -> State : grants[grant_id].runs_today.count += 1
else new day, cap > 0
Clause -> State : runs_today := {day: today, count: 1}
else exhausted
Clause --> API : abort "grant daily run cap exhausted"
API --> API : re-read grant -> **429 grant_caps_exceeded**
end
Clause -> State : runs[run_id] := {owner: grant.grantor,\ngrant_id, revision 0, status "running",\nhashes, events [runStarted]}
Clause -> State : put both states back (join closes)
Clause --> API : acknowledge true
API -> API : verify registration on the observer\n(grant_id link, hashes, revision 0), then\nresume the durable kernel
end

note over Deploy, API #FFF0C7
The classifier maps aborts honestly by RE-READING the public
grant record after the deploy errors: absence, revocation, and
cap exhaustion are knowable without authorization; whatever
remains is 500. Node-refused unfunded deploys surface earlier
as **402 deploy_unfunded**; an unobserved finality window is
**504 deploy_not_finalized** ("poll the run state").
end note
@enduml
